The '''Ogre Enclave''', located south-west of [[Yanille]] and accessed via the cave in the market of [[Gu'Tanoth]], is one of several locations containing [[Blue dragon]]s, and is visited during the [[Watchtower Quest]].

In the centre of the cave is the [[Rock of Dalgroth]], which you can mine during the [[Watchtower Quest]] for the [[Crystal (Watchtower)#Grey|grey crystal]].

While blue dragons and greater demons are present in the cave, they are rarely killed for Slayer purposes, as the dungeon is extremely far from a bank and other locations are more easily accessible.

A [[dwarf multicannon]] may be used here, but it is '''not''' a multi-combat area.

==Transportation==
If returning to this cave after completing the [[Watchtower Quest]], you will not need any [[cave nightshade]], as you can just sneak past the [[Enclave guard]]s without it. Also, you do not need a light source when entering the cave unlike the other [[Skavid]] caves nearby. To leave the cave, there is an exit in the centre of the north wall. It will take you to the north cave near the pathway to [[Gu'Tanoth]].
*Teleport to your house in Yanille (requires 50 [[Construction]]) and run west, then south to the entrance of Gu'Tanoth. Alternatively, if you have 39 [[Agility]], 38 [[Strength]] and 21 [[Ranged]], you can use a [[Mith grapple]] on the wall in south-west Yanille to take you right to the entrance of the city. With 69 Agility, this shortcut can be used without a grapple and without Strength or Ranged level requirement.
*Teleport to [[Castle Wars]] using a [[ring of dueling]] and run south over the bridge and then east to the entrance.
*If you have completed the Watchtower Quest, teleport to the [[Watchtower (building)|Watchtower]] using the [[Watchtower Teleport|spell]], run east and use the shortcut requiring level 16 Agility to get inside Yanille. Run south and use the grapple shortcut if you are able to.
*Use the [[Minigame]] interface to teleport to the [[Nightmare Zone]] and then run west through Yanille or over the south-east corner of the city to get to the entrance.
*There are two [[fairy ring]]s fairly close to the entrance. The one north-west of Yanille {{fairycode|CIQ}} and running south, or the one in Feldip Hills {{fairycode|AKS}} and running north (beware of Ogres and wolves).
*If you have completed [[One Small Favour]], you can use a [[gnome glider]] in the Feldip Hills and run north to the entrance.

