The '''Mourner Tunnels''' are located outside the basement of the [[Mourner Headquarters]] in the north-eastern part of [[West Ardougne]]. During [[Mourning's End Part II]], the [[Head Mourner]] gives the player the [[new key]], which can be used to enter the tunnels from the basement. Note that if the player is not wearing full [[mourner gear]], the [[mourner]]s in the basement will be [[Aggressiveness|aggressive]].

After the completion of Mourning's End Part II, the [[slayer ring]] can be used to teleport directly into the tunnels, skipping the need to wear mourner gear or have the new key. After the completion of [[Song of the Elves]], the mourners in the basement leave, and neither the key nor the mourner gear are required to use the basement door.
{{map|mtype=pin|2542,3327|caption=Trapdoor entrance to Mourner Tunnels.|align=right}}

==Points of interest==
===Dark beasts===
There are 19 [[dark beast]]s in the north-east and western parts of the first half of the tunnels. They are aggressive, attack quickly, and can deal a lot of damage.

===Runite===
The [[Mourner Tunnels mine]] contains a single [[runite rock]].

===The Temple of Light===
To the west of the tunnels is the entrance to the [[Temple of Light]]. During [[Mourning's End Part II]], the [[Head Mourner]] gives the player a [[new key]] in order to access the Mourner Tunnels allowing access to the [[Temple of Light]], and the [[Death Altar]] inside.

Before the entrance to the temple is a dead mourner who can be searched for [[Edern's journal]], detailing the life of a mourner called Nissyen Edern.


[[File:Mourner Tunnels & Temple of Light map.png|thumb|500px|centre|A map of the underground tunnels beneath Mourner HQ.]]

