The '''Wyvern Cave''' is a pair of ancient caverns found on [[Fossil Island]]. It contains [[wyvern]]s that were long thought to be extinct. The northern cavern is monitored by [[Weve]] ([[Steve]]'s son) who only allows players on a [[Slayer task]] to kill the wyverns inside; the wyverns in the southern cavern can be killed at any time.

A [[dwarf multicannon]] '''cannot''' be set up; attempting to do so will result in "Fungi start eating into the legs of your cannon; you quickly decide not to set it up here."

==Transportation==
To get to the cave players have several options: 
* The northern, task-only cave is is reached via the trapdoor found in the [[Mushroom Forest]] {{Map|3678,3854,title:Northern Cave (task only),icon:redPin|type=maplink|mtype=pin|text=}}. To get to the cave, use the [[digsite pendant]] to teleport to Fossil Island. Then use the [[Magic Mushtree]] to teleport to Mushroom Meadow. Finally run south to the trapdoor.
* The regular cave is found south of the [[Museum Camp]] {{Map|3746,3779,title:Southern Cave,icon:bluePin|type=maplink|mtype=pin|text=}}. To get to it, teleport to the [[Digsite]]. Travel to Fossil Island using the barge, run east past the bank, and then south-east into the cave.

==Appearance==
From the appearance of both caves, it is clear that [[dragonkin]] have previously inhabited the area. In the northern cave, a shrine can be found alongside what appears to be [[Bones (Dragonkin)#Light|skeletal remains]] of a dragonkin. Upon examining the shrine, the chatbox will state ''Forcae castil draekeun. Ortha lokur. Lith kletter ortha lokur. Draekeun fia Lithkren.''

Using translations found in ''RuneScape 3'', the examine text can be roughly translated as ''Forcae combine dragon. First steel. Superior green first steel. Dragon safe from Lithkren''. [[Forcae]] is the name of the dragonkin who created [[metal dragons]], while [[Lithkren]] is the name of a fortress built by [[Zorgoth]].

In addition, the southern cave contains three stone tables with the dragonkin symbol. Two are destroyed, but one in the north-east corner is fully intact, alongside the [[Bones (Dragonkin)|remains]] of what is presumed to be a dragonkin.
[[File:Wyvern Cave dragonkin shrine.png|thumb|220px|left|The [[Shrine (Wyvern Cave)|dragonkin shrine]] found in the northern cavern.]]
[[File:Wyvern Cave stone table.png|thumb|220px|none|The intact [[Table (Wyvern Cave)|stone table]] found in the southern cavern.]]


